<title>SWEDEN: Moody's says not about to upgrade Sweden.</title>
<headline>Moody's says not about to upgrade Sweden.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. ratings agency Moody's said on Wednesday it did not intend to upgrade Sweden's sovereign credit ratings, squashing market rumours of an upgrade.</p>
<p>&quot;The outlook for Sweden is stable,&quot; Moody's main Swedish analyst Kristin Lindow told Reuters. &quot;There is no truth in the rumours.&quot;</p>
<p>Sweden's current credit rating is AA3.</p>
<p>-- Charlotte Meynert, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
